is.",
  "publication_types": "Journal Article|Meta-Analysis|Systematic Review",
  "year": 2018,
  "sentences": [
   {
    "n": 1,
    "text": "BACKGROUND/PURPOSE: Hirschsprung-associated enterocolitis (HAEC) is a life-threatening complication of Hir
schsprung's disease."
   },
   {
    "n": 2,
    "text": "HAEC is reported to occur in 6-50% of patients preoperatively and in 2-35% postoperatively."
   },
   {
    "n": 3,
    "text": "The exact cause of HAEC is not fully understood, but disturbances of intestinal microbiota have recently b
een reported in patients with HAEC."
   },
   {
    "n": 4,
    "text": "In recent years, the administration of probiotics has been proposed to reduce the incidence of HAEC."
   },
   {
    "n": 5,
    "text": "We conducted a systematic review and meta-analysis to determine the effect of probiotics on postoperative 
HAEC."
   },
   {
    "n": 6,
    "text": "METHODS: A systematic literature search for relevant articles was performed in four databases using the co
mbinations of following terms \"probiotics\", \"microbiota\", \"enterocolitis\", \"Lactobacillus\", \"Bifidobacterium\"
, \"Saccharomyces\", \"Streptococcus\", and \"Hirschsprung disease/Hirschsprung's disease\" for studies published betwe
en 2002 and 2017."
   },
   {
    "n": 7,
    "text": "The relevant cohorts of the effect of probiotics in postoperative patients were systematically searched fo
r clinical outcomes."
   },
   {
    "n": 8,
    "text": "Odds ratio (OR) or standard mean difference (SMD) with 95% confidence intervals (CI) were calculated using
 standardized statistical methodology."
   },
   {
    "n": 9,
    "text": "RESULTS: The search strategy identified 1274 reports."
   },
   {
    "n": 10,
    "text": "Overall, five studies met defined inclusion criteria, reporting a total of 198 patients."
   },
   {
    "n": 11,
    "text": "Two studies were prospective multicenter randomized control trials."
   },
   {
    "n": 12,
    "text": "Lactobacillus, Bifidobacterium, Streptococcus, and Enterococcus were used as probiotics."
   },
   {
    "n": 13,
    "text": "The incidence of HAEC with/without probiotics was 22.6 and 30.5%, respectively, but this was not statistic
ally different (OR 0.72; 95% CI 0.37-1.39; P????.33)."
   },
   {
    "n": 14,
    "text": "CONCLUSION: This study shows that the administration of probiotics was not associated with a significant r
eduction in the risk of HAEC."
   },
   {
    "n": 15,
    "text": "Additional studies are required to understand more fully the role of microbiota and complex interactions t
hat cause HAEC."
   },
   {
    "n": 16,
    "text": "With increasing knowledge of the role of microbiota in HAEC, we are likely to understand better the potent
ial benefits of probiotics in this disease."
