   },
   {
    "n": 11,
    "text": "CONCLUSIONS: This review suggests that higher maternal Vit D levels during pregnancy may lead to higher Vi
t D levels in neonates and ultimately a lower risk of neonatal hyperbilirubinemia."
   }
  ]
