    "text": "The pooled 12-month primary patency rate was 73.5% (95% CI, 62.4%-84.6%; I2 = 93%, considerable heterogene
ity)."
   },
   {
    "n": 12,
    "text": "The pooled primary failure rate was 19.3% (95% CI, 14.1%-24.5%; I2 = 69% - substantial heterogeneity), and
 pooled early maturation was 84.2% (95% CI, 78.1%-90.4%; I2 = 73%, substantial heterogeneity)."
   },
   {
    "n": 13,
    "text": "Upper-arm AVFs demonstrated consistently higher maturation than forearm sites."
   },
   {
    "n": 14,
    "text": "Diabetes, small vessel calibre and central venous catheter dependence were the most common predictors of p
oor outcome."
   },
   {
    "n": 15,
    "text": "Intraoperative heparin significantly reduced early thrombosis (RR 0.36; 95% CI, 0.13-0.99), whereas fish o
il and aspirin had no measurable benefit."
