    "text": "Volume overload predictors were evaluated on a univariate and multivariate basis."
   },
   {
    "n": 7,
    "text": "RESULTS: A total of 388 patients (4F-PCC, n = 191; plasma, n = 197) were enrolled."
   },
   {
    "n": 8,
    "text": "Volume overload occurred in 34 (9%) patients (4F-PCC, n = 9; plasma, n = 25)."
   },
   {
    "n": 9,
    "text": "In univariate analyses, use of plasma (vs. 4F-PCC), use of nonstudy plasma and/or platelets, race, history
 of congestive heart failure (CHF), and history of renal disease were associated with volume overload."
   },
   {
    "n": 10,
    "text": "In multivariate analyses, use of plasma (vs. 4F-PCC), history of CHF, and history of renal disease were in
dependent volume overload predictors."
   },
   {
    "n": 11,
    "text": "In an additional analysis restricted to volume overload events recorded up to Day 7, only use of plasma (v
s. 4F-PCC) was an independent volume overload predictor."
   },
   {
    "n": 12,
    "text": "CONCLUSIONS: After adjusting for other potential risk factors, plasma use was independently associated wit
h a greater risk of volume overload than 4F-PCC in patients requiring urgent VKA reversal."
   }
  ]
